*******************************************************************************************                                                                                        **		Apple IIgs New ImageWriter Printer Driver                                        **                                                                                        **		File: metrics.aii -- Exclusive print record access and dimension calculations    **                                                                                        **		Written by Ben Koning                                                            **		Copyright (C) 1990 Apple Computer, Inc.                                          **                                                                                        *******************************************************************************************							include		'equates.aii'																					include		'm16.util'							include		'e16.print'							include		'm16.intmath'							include		'e16.quickdraw'							include		'm16.quickdraw'																		MetricsProc					proc		export*****************************************************************************************************                                                                                                  ** METRICS (PAGE MEASUREMENT) MODEL AND IMPLEMENTATION                                              **                                                                                                  ** All information related to page size, print quality, etc., options is stored in a data           ** structure called the Print Record, the memory for which is the application's responsibility      ** (a print record should be maintained with each document enacted on by an application so that     ** page setup information stays with a letter, drawing, etc.), and the contents of which are        ** the responsibility of the currently selected printer driver.                                     **                                                                                                  ** The routines in this module seek to isolate the rest of this printer driver from the specifics   ** of the contents of the user's print record.  They also arbitrate between the realms of page      ** measurements in inches and rectangle sizes in pixels.                                            **                                                                                                  ** There are a set of GetXXX and SetXXX routines below, which must be called rather than            ** modifying the print record directly.  Before a SetXXX completes, it causes a calculation         ** routine to be called which ensures that the print record stays self-consistent.                  **                                                                                                  ** The calculation routine uses the paper type and selected sizing options to find values for       ** several rectangles, used by applications as well as the rest of this driver, and stores them.    **                                                                                                  ** From the paper type, its paper dimensions are looked up from a table.  This information is       ** stored in the rPaper rectangle.  Thus dimensions could be different for Letter, Legal,           ** Envelope, etc.  The vertical dimension is used, for example, to set the page length so that      ** form feed works correctly (as returned by the GetPaperLength routine, for example).              ** rPaper is given in pixels.                                                                       **                                                                                                  ** Margins are subtracted from the rPaper rectangle to create the rPage rectangle, the actual       ** printable area inside a sheet of paper.  The first point of rPage is made the origin, so         ** that the first point of rPaper is negative.  rPage is given in pixels.                           **                                                                                                  ** Note that the sizing settings (Vertical Condense, Reduction, Page Gap) actually increase the     ** effective printing area.  They are not just effects settings which would affect only the         ** outcome of the printing.  In other words, selecting 50%-size means that the application can      ** give the user more drawing space, for example.  Also, Landscape means that the paper is still    ** inserted normally into the printer; just that the X & Y dimensions that the application sees     ** are reversed.  In other words, selecting Landscape means that a drawing application's rulers     ** show 11" left to right and 8" top to bottom for 8x11" paper.                                     **                                                                                                  ** The metrics calculations proceed as follows:                                                     **                                                                                                  ** 		Get resolution in pixels/inch from equates based on port/land orientation setting          ** 		If vertical condense, double y resolution                                                  ** 		If reduction, multiply x,y resolutions accordingly                                         ** 		If 320 mode, half x resolution                                                             ** 		Divide x,y resolutions by 2 to convert from Imaging resolution to rPage res (see below)    ** 		Get paper_x, paper_y, paper_gap size in inches from table based on paper type setting      ** 		Multiply dimensions by resolutions to convert dimensions to pixels                         ** 		rPaper gets physical page dimensions with rPage first point as origin                      ** 		rPage gets page dimensions minus a border based horizontally on equates and vertically     ** 			on the paper_gap and the page gap setting                                              ** 		Landscape orientation causes rPaper and rPage to have x & y exchanged                      **                                                                                                  ** In addition to providing the application with information about the printable area, the rPage    ** rectangle is used as the source rectangle during picture recording (QDAux's OpenPicture,         ** ClosePicture, DrawPicture, etc).  When DrawPicture is called, the playback rectangle may be      ** the same size or may be bigger to allow for higher quality printing (the GetImagingSize routine  ** returns the playback size based on rPage and the quality setting).                               **                                                                                                  ** Two pixel-level units are defined for internal use: "rPage" units and "Imaging" units.  RPage    ** dimensions change with respect to the option settings which increase printable area real estate, ** as described above, but remain constant with respect to the Standard or Better quality mode      ** setting.  Imaging units, on the other hand, are equal to rPage units with a scaling factor       ** applied to facilitate higher resolution when printing at denser dot pitches.  For example, if    ** rPage.X2 is "100" and the quality is "standard", then ImagingSize.X2 would be "100".  But if     ** rPage.X2 is "100" and the quality is "better", then ImagingSize.X2 could be "200".  Two          ** routines, "ConvertImgToRPageSize" and "ConvertRPageToImgSize", are provided as the exclusive     ** converters between these two units.  These routines are especially exempt from DP/print record   ** availability restrictions, because they may need to be called from within our QD bottleprocs,    ** for example.  Thus, in summary: rPage is the amount of pixels that the application sees for the  ** positioning of QD objects, while the Imaging size is the amount of pixels that the driver has    ** to deal with when playing back the picture containing these objects, thus obtaining high reso-   ** lution on the printed paper since there "are more dots" in QD objects, causing smoother curves.  **                                                                                                  *******************************************************************************************************STARTPRH: Call to use print record from hdl; sets up ParamLongA, allows pr rec access without hdl:*StartPRH					ldy			#4						;lock handle							lda			[printRecordHandle],y							ora			#$8000							sta			[printRecordHandle],y							lda			[printRecordHandle]		;deref to get ptr in ParamLongA							sta			ParamLongA+0							ldy			#2							lda			[printRecordHandle],y							sta			ParamLongA+2							lda			printRecordHandle+0		;save pr rec hdl for later use							sta			MostRecentPRH+0							lda			printRecordHandle+2							sta			MostRecentPRH+2							rts*Static variable holding recent pr rec handle so routines w/o prrec access can look anyway:MostRecentPRH				dc.l		0						;most recent print record handle																**FINISHPRH: Call this when done working with print record handle:*FinishPRH					ldy			#4							lda			[printRecordHandle],y							and			#$7FFF							sta			[printRecordHandle],y							rts			**InitPrintRecord: Fills user's print record with default values, for both ex- and internal use.*On entry, printRecordHandle should be set.*							export		InitPrintRecordInitPrintRecord				jsr			SetMiscNil				;advanced features to default NIL							lda			#paperTypeUsaLetter		;standard paper size							sta			OptionA							jsr			SetPaper							stz			OptionA					;default print style options...							jsr			SetVSize				;normal vertical size							jsr			SetReduction			;no reduction							jsr			SetPageGap				;no vertical page gap							jsr			SetOrientation			;portrait mode							jsr			SetColor				;no color							lda			#1							sta			OptionA							lda			#32767							sta			OptionB							jsr			SetPageRange			;print all pages							jsr			SetFeed					;automatic sheet feed							jsr			SetCopies				;one copy							lda			#2						;standard print quality							sta			OptionA							brl			SetQuality							**OPTION SETTING ROUTINES: These modify the user's print record in DP variable "printRecord". They*are called as a result of default, validate, style, or job calls.  They leave the print record in*an uncorrupted state.  Unlike the old driver, we rely only on the offsets provided in the include*file, for future portability.  The parameter to be set is passed in the DP variables "OptionA" and*"OptionB".  For boolean values (such as portrait/landscape, etc), 0 means the default option:**NOTE: These routines should be the only entities within this driver to modify the print record.*An internal coding, which makes sense by using 0 for default values, etc., is used to refer to*values of print record settings, and backward compatiblity may demand that certain values be stored*in a reverse or bizarre sense in the print record.  It is the purpose of these Get/Set routines*to perform any such translation.**SETMISCNIL: Initializes nonuser option switches and miscellaneous and normally-nil fields:							export		SetMiscNilSetMiscNil					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprVersion					;Version ID							lda			#VersionID							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprInfo+oiDev				;Device ID							lda			#DeviceID					;2=LQ (1=IW 3=LW)							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							lda			#0							;0,0 first coords of rPage							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh1							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;also 0 for initial wDev							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							shortm							ldy			#oprJob+obJDocLoop							lda			#$80						;Set byte for spool print method							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprJob+ofFromUser							lda			#1							;Set from-user field byte							sta			[ParamLongA],y							longm*							ldy			#owResScaling				;new wResScaling: 2 for IW							lda			#2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							lda			#0*							ldy			#oprJob+opIdleProc							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;Default NIL idleproc							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprJob+opFileName							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;(ACC 0) NIL pFileName							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#opFileBlockSize							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;(ACC 0) NIL NEW pFileBlockSize							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#opFileMemLimit							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;(ACC 0) NIL NEW pFileMemLimit							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#opCTable							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;(ACC 0) NIL NEW pCTable							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#opSCBList							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;(ACC 0) NIL NEW pSCBList							iny							iny							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETPAPER: Sets the paper type, used for calculating printable area dimensions:														export		SetPaperSetPaper					jsr 		StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETVSIZE: Sets vertical sizing, normal or 50% ("condensed") for correct font aspect ratio:							export		SetVSizeSetVSize					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							bne			@ClearIt								;reverse sense!							ora			#wDevVSize							bra			@StoreIt@ClearIt					and			#歡DevVSize@StoreIt					sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETREDUCTION: Sets 100/50% reduction in a compatible way using internal code 0/1, respectively:							export		SetReduction							;encoded in wierd waySetReduction				jsr			StartPRH								;in backward sense							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							;access wDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#歡DevReduction							;clear reduction bit							sta			[ParamLongA],y							lda			OptionA									;get option 0..1							bne			SetReductionIts50						;branch based on it*SetReductionIts100			ldx			#0										;"00" -> %reduction							lda			#wDevReduction							;"1"  -> wDev bit							bra			SetReductionSet*SetReductionIts50			ldx			#50										;"50" -> %reduction							lda			#0										;"0"  -> wDev bit*SetReductionSet				ora			[ParamLongA],y							;store wDev bit...							sta			[ParamLongA],y							;"wDev" offset in Y							ldy			#oprStl+oreduction						;store %reduction...							txa							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETPAGEGAP: Sets page gap (formfeed at end-of-page or run across perforation) setting:							export		SetPageGapSetPageGap					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							bne			@ClearIt								;reverse sense!							ora			#wDevGap							bra			@StoreIt@ClearIt					and			#歡DevGap@StoreIt					sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETORIENTATION: Sets portrait or landscape setting:							export		SetOrientationSetOrientation				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							bne			@ClearIt								;reverse sense!							ora			#wDevOrientation							bra			@StoreIt@ClearIt					and			#歡DevOrientation@StoreIt					sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETQUALITY: Sets print loop method and imaging size determinant:							export		SetQualitySetQuality					jsr			StartPRH							lda			OptionA				;(0=draft,1=faster,2=std,3=better)							ldy			#owQuality			;put code in new quality word...							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprStl+owDev		;now ensure wDev Better bit set right...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#歡DevBetterText							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							cpx			#3							bne			SeQuSetBJD							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ora			#wDevBetterText							sta			[ParamLongA],ySeQuSetBJD					lda			#$80				;now ensure bJDocLoop set right...							ldx			OptionA							bne			SeQuStoreBJD							lda			#$00SeQuStoreBJD				ldy			#oprJob+obJDocLoop							shortm							sta			[ParamLongA],y							longm							jsr			CalcAndFinishPRH							lda			OptionA				;if 0(draft), force modes...							bne			SeQuExit							jsr			SetReduction		;100%		;(OptionA is zero)							jsr			SetPageGap			;dfl vgap	;draft mode can deal with							jsr			SetOrientation		;portraitSeQuExit					rts*SETCOLOR: Sets color printing or grayscale conversion method:							export		SetColorSetColor					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			OptionA							beq			@ClearIt							ora			#wDevColor							bra			@StoreIt@ClearIt					and			#歡DevColor@StoreIt					sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETFEED: Sets manual page feed interrupt dialog enable flag:							export		SetFeedSetFeed						jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+ofeed							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETPAGERANGE: Sets range of pages to be processed (others are ignored and not recorded):														export		SetPageRange				;OptionA/B = first/last 1..xSetPageRange				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiFstPage							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprJob+oiLstPage							lda			OptionB							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH*SETCOPIES: Sets number of copies to produce for each page:														export		SetCopies					;OptionA = # copies 1..xSetCopies					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiCopies							lda			OptionA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							brl			CalcAndFinishPRH							CalcAndFinishPRH			jsr			CalcMetrics					;Common exit sequence							brl			FinishPRH															**INFORMATION INQUIRY ROUTINES: These routines return (possibly processed) info about pr rec items:*NOTE: These routines return data in EITHER accumulator OR zero flag status OR X/Y registers.*NOTE: These routines return 0 for the common default settings; may be inverse of wDev.**GETOKOURDRIVER: Sets zero flag (BEQ test) if DeviceID AND VersionID came from our driver:							export		GetOkOurDriverGetOkOurDriver				jsr			StartPRH					;get and lock handle							ldy			#oprInfo+oiDev				;DeviceID offset							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get it							cmp			#DeviceID					;zero flag set/clr if yes/no ours							bne			InqExitZFlag				;nope, was different printer							ldy			#oprVersion					;VersionID offset							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get it							cmp			#VersionID					;zero flag set/clr if yes/no oursInqExitZFlag				php										;zero flag set on exit							jsr			FinishPRH					;unlock handle							plp										;zero flag valid again							rts										;exit							*GETPAPER: Returns the paper type in the accumulator:							export		GetPaperGetPaper					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			[ParamLongA],yInqExitACC					pha							jsr			FinishPRH							pla							rts							*GETVSIZE: Gets vertical sizing (normal or condensed) in the zero flag (BEQ if normal size):							export		GetVSizeGetVSize					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevVSize							eor			#wDevVSize					;reverse sense of wDev bit!							brl			InqExitZFlag							*GETREDUCTION: Gets reduction value (100/50 => 0/1) in ACC from prrec-compatible encoding:							export		GetReduction				;stored backwards forGetReduction				jsr			StartPRH					;compatibility: stored as							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;"100/50 => 1/0"							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;access wDev...							and			#wDevReduction							bne			GetReductionIts100GetReductionIts50			lda			#1							;50% => return "1"							bra			InqExitACCGetReductionIts100			lda			#0							;100% => return "0"							bra			InqExitACC							*GETPAGEGAP: Gets page gap yes/no in the zero flag (BEQ if normal page gap, BNE if no gap):							export		GetPageGapGetPageGap					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevGap							eor			#wDevGap					;reverse sense of wDev bit!							brl			InqExitZFlag							*GETORIENTATION: Returns 1 in ACC if landscape, 0 if normal portrait:							export		GetOrientationGetOrientation				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevOrientation							eor			#wDevOrientation			;reverse sense of wDev bit!							beq			GetOrientation1							lda			#1GetOrientation1				brl			InqExitACC*GETQUALITY: Gets quality mode in ACC (0=draft(diff meth), 1=faster, 2=std, 3=better(hires)):							export		GetQualityGetQuality					jsr			StartPRH					;lock and dereference*							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;if wDev.Better=0 AND							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;our wQuality=3 -> force to 2...							and			#wDevBetterText							bne			GeQuForceTo3				;(if wDev.Better=1 -> force to 3)							ldy			#owQuality							lda			[ParamLongA],y							cmp			#3							bne			GeQuDoneNDQualGeQuForceTo2				lda			#2							;plA still points to wQuality							sta			[ParamLongA],y							bra			GeQuDoneNDQualGeQuForceTo3				lda			#3							ldy			#owQuality							sta			[ParamLongA],y				GeQuDoneNDQual*							ldy			#oprJob+objDocLoop			;if bjDocLoop=0 -> force to 0							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#$FF							cmp			#0							bne			GeQuDoneDQualGeQuForceTo0				lda			#0							ldy			#owQuality							sta			[ParamLongA],yGeQuDoneDQual*							ldy			#owQuality					;now get info from new place							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC					;unlock and exit with ACC set							*GETCOLOR: Gets color option in zero flag (BEQ if default no, we don't want color):							export		GetColorGetColor					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevColor							brl			InqExitZFlag							*GETFEED: Gets manual page feed option in zero flag (BEQ if manual page feed):							export		GetFeedGetFeed						jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+oFeed							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitZFlag							*GETPAGERANGE: Gets page range (First Page -> X; Last Page -> Y):							export		GetPageRangeGetPageRange				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiFstPage							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							ldy			#oprJob+oiLstPage							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							jsr			FinishPRH							ply							plx							rts*GETCOPIES: Gets number of copies to be printed in accumulator:							export		GetCopiesGetCopies					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+oiCopies							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC														*GETSPOOLFILENAMEPTR: Gets optional user-select spool filename ptr (lo->X, hi->Y, carry if not NIL):							export		GetSpoolFileNamePtrGetSpoolFileNamePtr			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+opFileNameInqExitWithXYPtrData		lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							iny							iny							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							jsr			FinishPRH							ply							plx							stx			ParamLongA							tya							ora			ParamLongA							cmp			#1							;set carry if not NIL pointer							rts*GETSPOOLMEMINC: Gets optional user-selectable mem inc value for spooling (lo->X, hi->Y, carry):							export		GetSpoolMemIncGetSpoolMemInc				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#opFileBlockSize							bra			InqExitWithXYPtrData*GETSPOOLMEMLEFTLIMIT: Gets optional user-selectable to-disk spool threshold (lo->X, hi->Y, carry):							export		GetSpoolMemLeftLimitGetSpoolMemLeftLimit		jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#opFileMemLimit							bra			InqExitWithXYPtrData							*GETIMAGERCTABLE: Gets optional user-select color table pointer for imaging (lo->X, hi->Y, carry):							export		GetImagerCTableGetImagerCTable				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#opCTable							bra			InqExitWithXYPtrData*GETIMAGERSCBLIST: Gets optional user-select SCB list pointer for imaging (lo->X, hi->Y, carry):							export		GetImagerSCBListGetImagerSCBList			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#opSCBList							bra			InqExitWithXYPtrData							*GETIDLEPROC: Gets optional user-select IdleProc called during imaging (lo->X, hi->Y, carry):							export		GetIdleProcGetIdleProc					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprJob+opIdleProc							bra			InqExitWithXYPtrData							*GETRPAGESIZE: Gets bottom right coordinates of last calculated rPage field in pixels (->X,Y):							export		GetRPageSizeGetRPageSize				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha							jsr			FinishPRH							ply							plx							rts*GETIMAGINGSIZE: Gets bottom right coordinates of how big the offscrn pix buff should be (->X,Y):							export		GetImagingSizeGetImagingSize				jsr			StartPRH					;lock print rec struct & deref							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2			;copy values first...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							sta			GeImSzX							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							sta			GeImSzY							lda			GeImSzX						;and then convert them...							jsr			ConvertRPageToImgSize							sta			GeImSzX							lda			GeImSzY							jsr			ConvertRPageToImgSize							sta			GeImSzYGeImSzDone					jsr			FinishPRH					;release print record							ldx			GeImSzX						;get results							ldy			GeImSzY							rtsGeImSzX						dc.w		0GeImSzY						dc.w		0*GETCRWIDTH: Gets our own internal calc abs right margin, always in max res printer pixels (->ACC):							export		GetCrWidthGetCrWidth					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#owPaperCrWidth							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC							*GETPAPERLENGTH: Gets vertical size of paper in draft-text-mode (72 vert dpi) pixels (->ACC):							export		GetPaperLengthGetPaperLength				jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType			;generate index for curr paper							lda			[ParamLongA],y							asl a							asl a							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							tax							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+2,x		;get paper type's vert size							ldx			#72							;do *72 and then /16							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert							brl			InqExitACC							*GETVGAPSIZE: Gets vertical gap size in draft-text-mode (72 vert dpi) pixels (->ACC):							export		GetVGapSizeGetVGapSize					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType			;doing (-1*(-GAP)*72)/16...							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;generate index for curr paper							asl a							asl a							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							tax							lda			#0							;got index, now do 0 - (-GAP)							sec							sbc			CalcMetricsPtTbl+4,x		;got GAP...							tax							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;...but zero if "no gaps" is on							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevGap					;prrec setting is reverse sense							bne			GetVGapSize1							ldx			#0GetVGapSize1				txa							ldx			#72							;do *72 and then /16							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert							brl			InqExitACC							*GETMODEBYTE: Gets 320/640 mode byte at the time of print record formation (->ACC):							export		GetModeByteGetModeByte					jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+ointernA							lda			[ParamLongA],y							brl			InqExitACC							*GETSTATMESGDISABLE: Gets if status message box is enabled/disabled, 0/1 respectively, in A:							export		GetStatMesgDisableGetStatMesgDisable			jsr			StartPRH							ldy			#oprStl+owDev							lda			[ParamLongA],y							and			#wDevNoStatusBox							beq			GeMdDone							lda			#1GeMdDone					brl			InqExitACC							*GETCONVERTQUALBITS: Converts print record information into QualityBits for imaging routine (->ACC):							export		GetConvertQualBitsGetConvertQualBits			lda			#0							;start all bits clr for ORA's							pha*GetConvertQualBits0			jsr			GetQuality					;check for Better mode							cmp			#3							beq			GetConvertQualBitsItsBett							cmp			#1							;check for Faster mode							bne			GetConvertQualBits1GetConvertQualBitsItsFast	pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%0110000000000000			;set img_qbit 13: 1=bi/鶴old							pha										;set img_qbit 14: 1=low res patt							bra			GetConvertQualBits1GetConvertQualBitsItsBett	pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%0000000000000001			;set imager_qbit 0: 1=Better							pha*GetConvertQualBits1			jsr			GetOrientation				;check orientation mode							cmp			#1							bne			GetConvertQualBits2							pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%0000000000000010			;set imager_qbit 1: 1=Landscape							pha*GetConvertQualBits2			jsr			GetVSize					;check Vertical Condense mode							beq			GetConvertQualBits3							pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%0000000000000100			;set imager_qbit 2: 1=VCondense							pha*GetConvertQualBits3			jsr			GetReduction				;check Reduction value 0/1							cmp			#1							bne			GetConvertQualBits4							pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%0000000000001000			;set imager_qbit 3: 1=50% Reduct							pha*GetConvertQualBits4			jsr			GetPageGap					;check Gap setting							beq			GetConvertQualBits5							pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%0000000010000000			;set imager_qbit 7: 1=No gap							pha*GetConvertQualBits5			jsr			GetColor					;check Color setting							beq			GetConverQualBitsDone							pla							;			  5432109876543210							ora			#%1000000000000000			;set imager_qbit 15: 1=Color							pha*GetConverQualBitsDone		pla							brl			InqExitACC					;exit with QualityBits in ACC**METRICS UNITS CONVERSION ROUTINES: These routines convert between application-level ("rPage")*and imaging-level ("Imaging") (which are possibly double-size) coordinate units.  These routines*do not assume any environment, such as a valid "printRecordHandle", or D/B environment, so they*can be called anywhere.  These routines should be the exclusive converters betwen these units.**CONVERTRPAGETOIMGSIZE: rPage -> Img [pict.source (small) -> pict.dest (big)] (input/output in ACC):							export		ConvertRPageToImgSizeConvertRPageToImgSize		phb										;save/setup B...							phk							plb							sta			CoRpCoordValue				;save input given in A							phd										;save/setup D...							pha							pha							tsc							ina							tcd*							lda			MostRecentPRH+0				;deref pr rec handle...							sta			<0							lda			MostRecentPRH+2							sta			<2							lda			[0]							tax							ldy			#2							lda			[0],y							sta			<2							stx			<0							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;get wDev data...							lda			[0],y*							tax										;do nothing if Better not set							and			#wDevBetterText							beq			CoRpDidAdjRed							txa*							and			#wDevReduction							beq			CoRpDidAdjRed				;cmp for "0" => 50%, else 100%CoRpIts100					asl			CoRpCoordValue				;100%: doubleCoRpDidAdjRed														;50%: leave alone*														pla										;restore D...							pla							pld							lda			CoRpCoordValue				;get result in A							plb										;restore B							rts										;exit with A set*CoRpCoordValue				dc.w		0							;storage for input/output param							*CONVERTIMGTORPAGESIZE: Img -> rPage [pict.dest (big) -> pict.source (small)] (input/output in ACC):							export		ConvertImgToRPageSizeConvertImgToRPageSize		phb										;save/setup B...							phk							plb							sta			CoImCoordValue				;save input given in A							phd										;save/setup D...							pha							pha							tsc							ina							tcd*							lda			MostRecentPRH+0				;deref pr rec handle...							sta			<0							lda			MostRecentPRH+2							sta			<2							lda			[0]							tax							ldy			#2							lda			[0],y							sta			<2							stx			<0							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;get wDev data...							lda			[0],y*							tax										;do nothing if Better not set							and			#wDevBetterText							beq			CoImDidAdjRed							txa*							and			#wDevReduction							beq			CoImDidAdjRed				;cmp for "0" => 50%, else 100%CoImIts100					lsr			CoImCoordValue				;100%: halve (undo double)CoImDidAdjRed														;50%: leave alone*							pla										;restore D...							pla							pld							lda			CoImCoordValue				;get result in A							plb										;restore B							rts										;exit with A set*CoImCoordValue				dc.w		0							;storage for input/output param**CALCMETRICS: This routine sets iH/Vres, crWidth, rPage and rPaper in print record based*on the option bit and page type settings in the print record.**NOTE: This is the only routine other than the Get/Set routines which may access the print record*directly, and thus is subject to backward print record flag compatibility issues.*							export		CalcMetricsCalcMetrics					jsr			StartPRH					;lock and dereference*Save wDev field for repeated use:							ldy			#oprStl+owDev				;get & save wDev for use...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							pha*Start with max possible port/land resolutions; equates assume Better/V.Condensed/100%/640:							ldx			#maxResPortraitX			;assume portrait orientation							stx			CaMeRawAcrossResolution		;P: for crWidth calc later							ldy			#maxResPortraitY/2			;P: default not V.Condensed							and			#wDevOrientation			;wDev still in acc							bne			CalcMetricsGotRawRes							ldx			#maxResLandscapeX			;no, it's landscape							ldy			#maxResLandscapeY			;L: for crWidth calc later							sty			CaMeRawAcrossResolution							ldy			#maxResLandscapeY/2			;L: default not V.CondensedCalcMetricsGotRawRes		stx			ParamWordA					;pwA & pwB will build iH/VRes							sty			ParamWordB*1 | 2 times X & Y resolutions if 100% | 50% life size (increases printable area):							pla										;get wDev...							pha							and			#wDevReduction							bne			CalcMetricsDidAdjRed		;cmp for "1" => 100%, else 50%CalcMetricsIts50			asl			ParamWordA					;50%: double...							asl			ParamWordBCalcMetricsDidAdjRed*2 times Y resolution if Vertical Condense mode is on (increases printable area):							pla										;get wDev...							pha							and			#wDevVSize							bne			CalcMetricsNotCondensed							asl			ParamWordB					;double Y resolution if VCCalcMetricsNotCondensed*1/2 X res if 320 mode.  Also, store mode bit in "internA" for future band buff alloc calc:							pha							_GetMasterSCB							pla							and			#$80							ldy			#oprStl+ointernA							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;320/640 mode -> oprStl.internA							cmp			#$80							beq			CalcMetricsNot320			;branch if 640 mode active							lsr			ParamWordA					;half X resolution if 320 modeCalcMetricsNot320*1/2 of X & Y resolution always; pixel addressability is always as if not in Better mode:							lsr			ParamWordA					;divide X by 2							lsr			ParamWordB					;divide Y by 2*We now have effective iHres and iVres that will be produced by imager in printer-pixels per inch:							ldy			#oprInfo+oiHres							lda			ParamWordA							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+oiVres							lda			ParamWordB							sta			[ParamLongA],y*Now that we have iH&Vres, we will calculate rPage&rPaper&crWidth in inch*16 based on paper type:*Get dimensions of current paper type:							ldy			#oprStl+opaperType							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;get paper type ID							cmp			#maxPaperTypeID+1			;make sure it's in range							bcc			CalcMetricsPtOk							lda			#0							;else assume type 0							sta			[ParamLongA],yCalcMetricsPtOk				asl	a									;paper type * 6							asl a							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							clc							adc			[ParamLongA],y							tax										;index into paper dimension table							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+0,x		;get X dimension in 1/16th inches							sta			CaMeRawPaperWidth			;save paper real estate dimension							sta			ParamWordC					;paper X size in ParamWordC							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+2,x		;get Y dimension							sta			ParamWordD					;paper Y size in ParamWordD							lda			CalcMetricsPtTbl+4,x		;get -GAP value							sta			ParamWordE					;paper -GAP size in ParamWordE*If Gap option is turned off, zero our looked-up page -1*GAP value (GAP increases printable area):							pla										;get wDev...							pha							and			#wDevGap							bne			CalcMetricsYesGap			;branch if we DO have vert gap							stz			ParamWordE					;else, no gap: zero gap valueCalcMetricsYesGap*Calc internal and external versions of crWidth abs right margin, used for landscp right limit, etc:							ldx			CaMeRawAcrossResolution		;get physical resolution							lda			CaMeRawPaperWidth			;get amount of paper under head							sec							sbc			#(2*printLineMargin)		;...minus left&right margins							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;do (acc*x)/16							ldy			#owPaperCrWidth				;now store it in print record...							sta			[ParamLongA],y							lda			#prRecCrWidth				;also store the constant crWidth							ldy			#oprStl+ocrWidth			;value which apps have come to							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;expect in the print record...*rPaper.X1 = 0 - printLineMargin (black mark on bail) (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrt):							lda			#((孿rintLineMargin)+1)		;-1*printLineMargin always							ldy			#orPaper+oh1				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y*rPaper.X2 = rPaper.X1 + paper_size.X (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrait):							clc										;X1 still in acc							adc			ParamWordC					;add X size of paper type							ldy			#orPaper+oh2				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y*rPaper.Y1 = 0 - GAP (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrait):							lda			ParamWordE					;get -1*GAP for current paper							ldy			#orPaper+ov1				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y*rPaper.Y2 = rPaper.Y1 + paper_size.Y (rPage.X1.Y1=0,0 is origin) (assuming Portrait):							clc										;Y1 still in acc							adc			ParamWordD					;add Y size of paper type							ldy			#orPaper+ov2				;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y*rPage.X1 and rPage.Y1 are both zero and are the origin for all other rPage/rPaper coordinates:							lda			#0							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh1							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y*rPage.X2 = paper_size.X - 2*printLineMargin (black mark on bail) (assuming Portrait):							lda			ParamWordC					;get X size of paper type							sec										;subtract for left&right border							sbc			#2*printLineMargin							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2			;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y*rPage.Y2 = paper_size.Y - 2*GAP value (assuming Portrait):							lda			ParamWordE					;get gap value (-1*GAP or 0)							clc							adc			ParamWordE					;now it's -2*GAP							clc										;add Y size of paper type; now...							adc			ParamWordD					;...we've done paperY-2*GAP							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2			;store it							sta			[ParamLongA],y*If Landscape orientation, rotate&mirror by exchanging rPage&rPaper X and Y coordinates:							pla										;get wDev...							pha							and			#wDevOrientation			;if portrait, leave coords alone							bne			CalcMetricsNoFlip			;else flip them:*							ldy			#orPaper+ov1				;rPaper.X1 <-> Y1...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							tax							ldy			#orPaper+oh1							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#orPaper+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y							txa							ldy			#orPaper+oh1							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#orPaper+ov2				;rPaper.X2 <-> Y2...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							tax							ldy			#orPaper+oh2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#orPaper+ov2							sta			[ParamLongA],y							txa							ldy			#orPaper+oh2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2			;rPage.X2 <-> Y2...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							tax							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							sta			[ParamLongA],y							txa							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							sta			[ParamLongA],yCalcMetricsNoFlip*Right now, rPage/rPaper are in values of inch*16. Now convert all of these to the printing pixels*that the application sees by signed multiply by iHres/iVres and signed divide by 16:							ldy			#orPaper+oh1				;get value just computed above...							lda			[ParamLongA],y				;in a-reg. This is negative!							eor			#$FFFF						;negate it...							clc										;...so the unsigned convert...							adc			#1							;...will work correctly							ldx			ParamWordA					;get resolution A)iHres B)iVres							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper X1							eor			#$FFFF						;negate it...							clc										;...again...							adc			#1							;...back to negative							ldy			#orPaper+oh1				;store value just converted...							sta			[ParamLongA],y				;back into print record*														ldy			#orPaper+ov1							lda			[ParamLongA],y							eor			#$FFFF						;negate -> positive							clc							adc			#1							ldx			ParamWordB							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper Y1							eor			#$FFFF						;negate -> negative							clc							adc			#1							ldy			#orPaper+ov1							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#orPaper+oh2				;all others are all positive...							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordA							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper X2							ldy			#orPaper+oh2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#orPaper+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordB							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPaper Y2							ldy			#orPaper+ov2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordA							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPage X2							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+oh2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*														ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							lda			[ParamLongA],y							ldx			ParamWordB							jsr			CalcMetricsConvert			;convert rPage Y2							ldy			#oprInfo+orPage+ov2							sta			[ParamLongA],y*Copy the PrInfo subrecord to PrInfoPT for compatibility reasons:							ldy			#oprInfo+12					;source: prInfo offset							ldx			#oprInfoPT+12				;destination: prInfoPT offsetCaMeCopyPrInfoLp			lda			[ParamLongA],y				;length: 14 bytes							phy							txy							sta			[ParamLongA],y							ply							dex							dex							dey							dey							cpy			#oprInfo							bcs			CaMeCopyPrInfoLp*Exit:							pla										;get rid of wDev on stack							brl			FinishPRH					;return via lock routine*Static variables:CaMeRawAcrossResolution		dc.w		0							;for crWidth calculationCaMeRawPaperWidth			dc.w		0							;for crWidth calculation**The following routine does AREG := (AREG*XREG)/16 with unsigned arithmetic:*CalcMetricsConvert			pha										;Space for multiply result...							pha										;...longspace							pha										;A REG: value to be converted							phx										;X REG: resolution iHres/iVres							_Multiply							pulllong	ParamLongB							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB					;divide by 2 lo word	=/2							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB					;divide by 2 lo word	=/4							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB					;divide by 2 lo word	=/8							lsr			ParamLongB+2				;divide by 2 hi word							ror			ParamLongB					;divide by 2 lo word	=/16							lda			ParamLongB					;get lo word only							rts										;we're done							**Lookup table containing physical dimensions (in inch * 16) of different types of paper:*CalcMetricsPtTbl			dc.w		paperSizeUsaLetterX			;indexed if paper type == 0							dc.w		paperSizeUsaLetterY			;type 0 must be US Letter							dc.w		-1*paperSizeUsaLetterGap							dc.w		paperSizeUsaLegalX			;indexed if paper type == 1							dc.w		paperSizeUsaLegalY			;type 1 must be US Legal							dc.w		-1*paperSizeUsaLegalGap														dc.w		paperSizeEurA4X				;indexed if paper type == 2							dc.w		paperSizeEurA4Y				;type 2 must be A4 Letter							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEurA4Gap														dc.w		paperSizeEurIntlFanfoldX	;indexed if paper type == 3							dc.w		paperSizeEurIntlFanfoldY	;type 3 must be Intl Fanfold							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEurIntlFanfoldGap							dc.w		paperSizeEurB5X				;indexed if paper type == 4							dc.w		paperSizeEurB5Y							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEurB5Gap							dc.w		paperSizeUsaStatementX		;indexed if paper type == 5							dc.w		paperSizeUsaStatementY							dc.w		-1*paperSizeUsaStatementGap														dc.w		paperSizeEnvNo6X			;indexed if paper type == 6							dc.w		paperSizeEnvNo6Y							dc.w		-1*paperSizeEnvNo6Gap							dc.w		paperSizeLblSmlX			;indexed if paper type == 7							dc.w		paperSizeLblSmlY							dc.w		-1*paperSizeLblSmlGap							dc.w		paperSizeLblMedX			;indexed if paper type == 8							dc.w		paperSizeLblMedY							dc.w		-1*paperSizeLblMedGap							dc.w		paperSizeLblLrgX			;indexed if paper type == 9							dc.w		paperSizeLblLrgY							dc.w		-1*paperSizeLblLrgGap														dc.w		paperSizeLblPackingX		;indexed if paper type == 10							dc.w		paperSizeLblPackingY							dc.w		-1*paperSizeLblPackingGap														dc.w		paperSizeLblDisk35X			;indexed if paper type == 11							dc.w		paperSizeLblDisk35Y							dc.w		-1*paperSizeLblDisk35Gap														dc.w		paperSizeLblDisk525X		;indexed if paper type == 12							dc.w		paperSizeLblDisk525Y							dc.w		-1*paperSizeLblDisk525Gap							endproc							end